      "content": "Thanks for those. I noticed a pretty big contrast in the tone. For the first part, you used words like \"primal\" and \"raw,\" while the second part uses \"disciplined logic\" and \"structured brilliance.\" \n\nI want to make sure the exhibit doesn't feel too lopsided. Could you expand on the first section? I want to dive deeper into why those indigenous methods are described that way—is it because they were more intuitive or instinctual compared to the \"structured\" European approach?",
